# DECISION RECORD, 2026-09-26 (docs/explanation/confidentiality-guards.md, « Decisions and
# deviations »). The session trailers below stay in main's history rather than being expunged.
# SLSA v1.2 source track, « Safe Expunging Process », asks that content removal follow a documented
# process; the process here concluded not to remove, for three reasons. A rewrite does not remove
# the text from forks, from cached pull request refs or from anywhere a commit id was already
# quoted (GitHub's « Removing sensitive data from a repository »). Branch protection forbids the
# force push a rewrite needs, and lifting it is a larger risk than the text. And each address
# points to a PRIVATE session that no public reader can open; what it leaks is that the owner used
# Claude Code, which the attribution trailers on the same commits already say.
